267	<!-- ═══════════ SECTION 3: TOPIC & MESH ANALYSIS ═══════════ -->
268	<div class="section" id="topic-and-mesh-analysis">
269	  <h2>3. Research Topic &amp; MeSH Keyword Analysis</h2>
270	  <p class="section-obj">Most prevalent major topics and MeSH keywords, trending and emerging research areas, and topic shifts between years.</p>
271	
272	  <div class="callout amber">
273	    <strong>Data Note:</strong> 47.1% of records (n=2,303) have an empty <code>major_topic</code> field — common for newer publications not yet MeSH-indexed. The keyword field (<code>keywords</code>) has broader coverage and is used to supplement the topic analysis. Topic growth rates are computed as the change in normalized publication rate per 1,000 publications between 2024 and 2025, accounting for the overall volume decline.
274	  </div>
275	
276	  <div class="chart-row">
277	    <div class="chart-wrap">
278	      <h3>Top 20 Major MeSH Topics</h3>
279	      <canvas id="chart-topics-bar"></canvas>
280	    </div>
281	    <div class="chart-wrap">
282	      <h3>Topic Growth: Normalized Rate Change (2024→2025)</h3>
283	      <canvas id="chart-topics-growth"></canvas>
284	    </div>
285	  </div>
286	
287	  <h3>Fastest-Growing Keyword Clusters</h3>
288	  <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:12px;">
289	    Keywords with the largest increase in normalized appearance rate (per 1,000 publications) from 2024 to 2025, filtered for keywords appearing ≥5 times in 2024.
290	  </p>
291	  <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-width:700px;">
292	    <canvas id="chart-keywords-growth"></canvas>
293	  </div>
294	
295	  <h3>Top 30 Most Frequent MeSH Keywords</h3>
296	  <div class="chart-wrap" style="max-width:700px;">
297	    <canvas id="chart-keywords-top"></canvas>
298	  </div>
299	
300	  <h3>Key Observations</h3>
301	  <table>
302	    <tr><th>Observation</th><th>Detail</th></tr>
303	    <tr><td>COVID-19 remains predominant</td><td>Despite the pandemic's acute phase ending, COVID-19 is the #1 major topic (43 publications). Its normalized rate declined from 9.4/1K (2024) to 6.8/1K (2025), suggesting gradual normalization of pandemic-related research output.</td></tr>
304	    <tr><td>Chronic disease research dominates</td><td>Diabetes Mellitus Type 2, Breast Neoplasms, Alzheimer Disease, and Heart Failure rank among the top topics, reflecting the sustained research emphasis on non-communicable diseases with high global disease burden.</td></tr>
305	    <tr><td>Microbiome and omics rising</td><td>Gastrointestinal Microbiome (16 publications) and MicroRNAs (11) indicate strong interest in molecular-level and systems-biology approaches. These topics are trend-sensitive and may expand further as 2025–2026 indexing catches up.</td></tr>
306	    <tr><td>Coleoptera as an outlier</td><td>Coleoptera (beetles) appears as a top-10 major topic (10 publications), likely reflecting biodiversity/entomology research. Its normalized rate increased from 1.8/1K (2024) to 4.1/1K (2025) — the highest growth rate among topics with 2025 data.</td></tr>
307	    <tr><td>Keyword-level growth signals</td><td>Keywords like "Animal Structures" (+13.1/1K), "Animal Distribution" (+12.7/1K), and "Body Size" (+10.8/1K) show outsized normalized growth, suggesting increasing biodiversity and zoological research output. "Air Pollutants" keywords (+8.3/1K) signal growing environmental health research. "Molecular Dynamics Simulation" (+5.0/1K) reflects computational methods adoption.</td></tr>
308	    <tr><td>Demographic keywords dominate</td><td>"Humans", "Male", "Female", "Animals", and "Adult" are the most frequent MeSH keywords, consistent with the clinical and population-health orientation of PubMed-indexed research.</td></tr>
309	  </table>
310	</div>
