207	  <h2>1. Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</h2>
208	  <p class="section-obj">Monthly and yearly distribution of publications, accounting for the natural skew toward 2024 due to PubMed indexing lag. Volume trends, seasonality, and acceleration patterns are examined.</p>
209	
210	  <div class="callout amber">
211	    <strong>Data Note:</strong> Approximately 80.3% of records in this dataset are from 2024, reflecting real-world PubMed indexing patterns where older publications accumulate more indexed entries over time. The 2025 and 2026 figures represent partial-year data — 2026 covers only Q1 (Jan–Mar). All cross-year comparisons use normalized metrics. Additionally, 15.4% of records (n=754) have an unknown publication month and are excluded from monthly-level charts.
